    cta={{"href": "/free-seo-audit/", "label": "Book my free audit"}}
    glance={{"heading": "At a glance", "points": ["The audit covers four things: technical set-up, content quality, local search presence and AI search readiness.", "You get a prioritised 90-day action plan, with competitor benchmarking and a content gap analysis.", "It takes five to ten working days, depending on the size of your site.", "A free, shorter audit is available first if you want a look before paying."], "facts": [{"k": "Price", "v": "£750 fixed fee"}, {"k": "Turnaround", "v": "5 to 10 working days"}, {"k": "You receive", "v": "Report and 90-day action plan"}, {"k": "Free option", "v": "Free SEO audit, 2 to 3 working days"}, {"k": "Reply time", "v": "Within one working day"}, {"k": "Company", "v": "ND Media Ltd, no. 10784524", "href": "https://find-and-update.company-information.service.gov.uk/company/10784524"}]}}
  >
    <Fragment slot="title">SEO audit for <span class="mark">Guildford</span> businesses</Fragment>
  </PageHero>

  <article class="doc">
  <div class="prose">

    <div class="reveal">
    <h2>What my SEO audit covers</h2>

    <p>A comprehensive audit is a manual review, not a tool export. I look at your site from three angles: what Google can crawl and index, what a visitor sees, and what competitors do better. Findings fall into four areas.</p>

    <dl class="def-grid not-prose">
  <div><dt>Technical</dt><dd>Full technical crawl, Google Search Console data analysis, and Core Web Vitals assessment across mobile and desktop.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Content</dt><dd>Content quality evaluation against competitor benchmarks, plus a keyword gap analysis for your target terms.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Local</dt><dd>Local SEO profile review: Google Business Profile, citations, and local pack eligibility.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>AI Search</dt><dd>AI search readiness check covering ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Google AI Overview visibility.</dd></div>
</dl>

    <p>Every audit closes with a prioritised action plan, each recommendation ranked by estimated impact and implementation effort.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
    <h2>Why Guildford businesses need an SEO audit</h2>

    <p>Guildford sits at the intersection of technology, education, and high-value professional services. A solicitor on <strong>Guildford High Street</strong> needs accurate lead tracking before assigning value to rankings. A property agency covering the borough needs listing pages that remain crawlable as inventory changes. A technology company on <strong>Surrey Research Park</strong> needs fast, well-structured pages for enterprise buyers researching complex services.</p>

    <p>These are the patterns I see most often:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Websites where many pages are not indexed by Google, despite appearing entirely normal to visitors.</li>
      <li>Sites passing desktop speed tests but failing mobile Core Web Vitals. Google measures performance on mobile.</li>
      <li>Local businesses with inconsistent Name, Address, Phone (NAP) data across directories. This suppresses local pack visibility.</li>
      <li>Content that targets keywords with negligible local search volume while ignoring terms that Guildford residents actually search.</li>
      <li>Technical problems introduced by CMS updates, plugin conflicts, or hosting changes that went undetected for months.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>An audit replaces guesswork with evidence: a factual account of where the site stands and a ranked list of what to fix first.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
    <h2>Technical audit components</h2>

    <p>The technical audit examines your website's infrastructure, the foundation that determines whether search engines can access and understand your content. My <a href="/technical-seo-guildford/">technical SEO service</a> covers implementation. The audit identifies every issue as a necessary first step.</p>

    <ChecklistFigure title="Technical audit components" items={["Crawlability and indexation", "Site speed and Core Web Vitals", "URL architecture and internal linking", "Structured data validation", "Security and HTTPS"]} caption="Each is covered in detail below." />

    <h3>Crawlability and indexation</h3>

    <p>I crawl your entire site and compare discovered pages against Google Search Console's index coverage report. This reveals three groups of pages. Google cannot find some (orphaned content). Google finds but declines to index others (quality threshold failures). Google indexes some that you would prefer it did not (index bloat from tag pages, parameters or thin content).</p>

    <h3>Site speed and Core Web Vitals</h3>

    <p>I test every page template against Google's Core Web Vitals thresholds: Largest Contentful Paint under 2.5 seconds, Interaction to Next Paint under 200 milliseconds, and Cumulative Layout Shift under 0.1. I use both lab data (controlled testing) and field data (real user measurements from Chrome User Experience Report) because they frequently tell different stories.</p>

    <h3>URL architecture and internal linking</h3>

    <p>I map your site's URL structure, internal link graph, and crawl depth. Pages buried more than three clicks from the homepage receive less crawl priority and less link equity. I identify orphaned pages, redirect chains, broken links, and cannibalisation where multiple pages compete for the same keyword.</p>

    <h3>Structured data validation</h3>

    <p>I audit every schema markup implementation on your site. Incorrect structured data can result in manual actions from Google. Missing structured data means missed opportunities for rich results. I validate syntax, check for required properties, and identify schema types relevant to your business that have not yet been implemented.</p>

    <h3>Security and HTTPS</h3>

    <p>I verify HTTPS, check for mixed content, audit security headers and confirm HTTP to HTTPS redirects are clean. HTTPS is a Google ranking signal; the rest protects visitors and must not conflict with SEO changes.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
    <h2>Content audit components</h2>

    <p>Technical infrastructure ensures your pages are crawled and indexed; content quality determines where they rank. The content audit evaluates every page against Google's quality standards and your competitors' content.</p>

    <ChecklistFigure title="Content audit components" items={["Thin and duplicate content analysis", "Keyword targeting and search intent", "Content depth and topical authority", "Title tags and meta descriptions"]} caption="Each is covered in detail below." />

    <h3>Thin and duplicate content analysis</h3>

    <p>I identify three kinds of weak page. Some have insufficient unique content (under 300 words with no supporting media). Some are near-duplicates that cannibalise one another's rankings. Some are boilerplate-heavy because template content outweighs unique content. Each finding includes a specific recommendation: consolidate, expand, noindex, or remove.</p>

    <h3>Keyword targeting and search intent</h3>

    <p>I analyse which keywords each page currently targets (based on title tags, headings and content). I compare these against actual search queries driving impressions in Google Search Console. I then identify misalignments where your content does not match what searchers expect. I also identify keyword gaps, valuable searches your competitors rank for but you do not.</p>

    <h3>Content depth and topical authority</h3>

    <p>Google rewards sites that demonstrate comprehensive coverage of their subject area. I assess your topical authority by mapping your content against the full semantic field of your target topics. Gaps in coverage indicate missed ranking opportunities and reduced authority signals.</p>

    <h3>Title tags and meta descriptions</h3>

    <p>I audit every title tag. I check length (under 60 characters to avoid truncation), keyword placement, click-through rate potential and uniqueness. Duplicate or generic titles suppress CTR and waste ranking positions. Meta descriptions are reviewed for compelling, measured copy that encourages clicks from search results.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="not-prose my-12 py-8 border-y border-border">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Quick enquiry</p>
      <p class="font-heading text-brand text-xl mb-4">See exactly where your site stands.</p>
      <QuickForm heading="" subject="SEO Guildford: Audit mid-page enquiry" />
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
    <h2>Local SEO audit components</h2>

    <p>Local search visibility often drives the highest-value traffic for businesses serving Guildford and surrounding Surrey towns. The local audit examines every factor that affects your visibility in Google's local pack and map results.</p>

    <ChecklistFigure title="Local SEO audit components" items={["Google Business Profile", "Citation consistency", "Local content and landing pages", "Review profile"]} caption="Each is covered in detail below." />

    <h3>Google Business Profile</h3>

    <p>Google documents local ranking as relevance, distance and prominence. Your profile is the part you control most. I check completeness, categories, photos, reviews, posts and that the service area matches where you work.</p>

    <h3>Citation consistency</h3>

    <p>Your business name, address, and phone number must be identical across every directory, social profile, and mention on the web. I audit your citations across major UK directories (Yell, Thomson Local, Yelp, FreeIndex, Cylex) and industry-specific platforms, since inconsistencies confuse Google and suppress local rankings.</p>

    <h3>Local content and landing pages</h3>

    <p>I evaluate whether your site has sufficient local content to demonstrate genuine relevance to Guildford and surrounding areas. This includes location-specific service pages, local case studies, area guides, and geo-modified keyword targeting. Thin location pages that differ only by town name are flagged as a risk.</p>

    <h3>Review profile</h3>

    <p>I analyse your review volume, recency, rating distribution, and response rate across Google and relevant platforms. Review signals influence local rankings directly. I benchmark your profile against local competitors to identify gaps in your review acquisition approach.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
    <h2>AI search readiness audit</h2>

    <p>ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews and Copilot answer some queries directly and name sources. Google says no special file or markup is needed to appear in AI Overviews; the page has to be indexed and useful.</p>

    <p>My AI search readiness audit examines:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Whether your content appears in AI-generated answers for your target queries.</li>
      <li>Content structure and formatting that AI systems can extract and cite.</li>
      <li>Whether the right crawlers can reach your pages: Googlebot for AI Overviews, OAI-SearchBot for ChatGPT search, PerplexityBot for Perplexity.</li>
      <li>Entity markup that helps AI systems understand your business and expertise.</li>
      <li>Citation patterns in competitor AI mentions.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>My <a href="/ai-search-optimisation/">AI search optimisation service</a> covers the fixes. Evidence for what gets cited is in my <a href="/generative-engine-optimisation-uk/">GEO guide</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
    <h2>What you receive</h2>

    <p>The audit deliverable is a structured report rather than a raw data dump. Every finding is explained in clear language with a specific recommendation and priority level.</p>

    <h3>Deliverables</h3>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Executive summary.</strong> A one-page overview of your site's current SEO health, the top five priorities and the estimated impact of addressing them.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical audit report.</strong> Every crawl, speed, indexation, and structured data issue with severity rating and detailed fix instructions.</li>
      <li><strong>Content audit report.</strong> Page-by-page assessment of content quality, keyword targeting, and competitive positioning.</li>
      <li><strong>Local SEO report.</strong> GBP audit, citation accuracy check, and local ranking factor analysis.</li>
      <li><strong>AI search readiness report.</strong> Current AI visibility status and recommendations for improvement.</li>
      <li><strong>Prioritised action plan.</strong> Every recommendation is ranked by expected impact and implementation effort. You know precisely what to address first.</li>
      <li><strong>Walkthrough call.</strong> A 60-minute video call to review findings, answer questions, and discuss implementation options at your convenience.</li>
    </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
    <h2>How you might use the audit</h2>

    <p>With no in-house developer, the usual route is the audit followed by a monthly plan to implement it.</p>

    <p>With a development team, the audit works as a specification they implement in their own sprints. I am on call for questions.</p>

    <p>On a site with thousands of pages, the ranking tells you which sections to fix first. Full implementation can take months.</p>

    <p>The audit separates technical, content and competitive causes of lost rankings. This stops you spending on the wrong one.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
    <h2>Free vs comprehensive SEO audit</h2>

    <p>I offer a <a href="/free-seo-audit/">free SEO audit</a> that provides a high-level overview of your site's principal issues. It is useful for identifying whether your site has significant problems and for understanding the general state of your SEO.</p>

    <p>The paid audit goes deeper, as the table below shows. UK audit prices are compared in the <a href="/seo-cost-uk/">UK SEO cost guide</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto not-prose my-6 reveal" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Free and comprehensive website audit comparison table">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border border-border">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col" class="text-left p-3 border-b-2 border-border font-mono uppercase tracking-wide text-xs font-medium">Feature</th>
            <th scope="col" class="text-center p-3 border-b-2 border-border font-mono uppercase tracking-wide text-xs font-medium">Free Audit</th>
            <th scope="col" class="text-center p-3 border-b-2 border-border font-mono uppercase tracking-wide text-xs font-medium">Comprehensive Audit</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-border">Automated crawl scan</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">Yes</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-border">Manual expert review</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">No</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-border">Google Search Console analysis</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">No</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-border">Server log analysis</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">No</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-border">Competitor benchmarking</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">No</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-border">Content gap analysis</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">No</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-border">Local SEO profile audit</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">Basic</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">Comprehensive</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-border">AI search readiness</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">No</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-border">Prioritised action plan</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">Top 5 issues</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">All issues ranked</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="p-3 border-b border-border">Walkthrough call</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">No</td><td class="text-center p-3 border-b border-border">60 minutes</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="sm:hidden text-xs text-text-muted mt-2">Swipe horizontally to compare every audit feature.</p>

    <p>The free audit tells you there is a problem. The comprehensive audit tells you precisely what the problem is, how to resolve it, and in what order.</p>

    <div class="reveal">
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How long does an SEO audit take?</summary>
        <p>A comprehensive SEO audit for a Guildford business takes five to ten working days depending on site size. A 50-page professional services site typically takes around five days. E-commerce or property listing sites with thousands of pages require up to ten days for thorough analysis.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What is the difference between a free and paid SEO audit?</summary>
        <p>A free SEO audit provides a high-level summary of your site's principal issues using automated tools. A paid audit includes manual expert analysis and server log review. It also covers competitor benchmarking, content gap analysis and a prioritised action plan with implementation guidance. The paid audit tells you exactly what to fix and in what order.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Do I need an SEO audit if my site is already ranking?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Ranking today does not mean the site is sound. An audit finds risks before a core update exposes them and lists pages that could rank higher.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Will you implement the audit recommendations?</summary>
        <p>The audit is a standalone deliverable. Implementation is available as a separate engagement. Many Guildford businesses commission the audit first, review the findings at their leisure, and then engage me for implementation. Alternatively, your in-house team or developers can implement using my detailed specifications.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How often should a Guildford business commission an SEO audit?</summary>
        <p>I recommend a comprehensive audit annually, with quarterly technical health checks in between. An immediate audit is warranted regardless of schedule after a major redesign, a CMS migration or a sudden ranking decline.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What tools do you use for the audit?</summary>
        <p>I employ professional crawling tools, Google Search Console data and server log analysis. I add Core Web Vitals testing (both lab and field data), structured data validators and manual review. No single tool catches everything. That is precisely why my audits combine automated scanning with expert analysis.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What determines the price of an SEO audit?</summary>
        <p>SEO audit pricing depends primarily on site size, audit depth and the level of manual expert analysis involved. An automated report with minimal human review sits at the lower end of the market. A comprehensive audit combines automated crawl data with manual analysis, competitor benchmarking and business context. It commands a higher fee because it identifies issues that automated tools alone miss.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What is the difference between an SEO audit and ongoing SEO management?</summary>
        <p>An SEO audit is a one-time diagnostic that identifies what is wrong and ranks it by priority. Ongoing SEO management is the continuous work of implementing fixes, publishing content, building links and monitoring rankings over months. Many businesses commission an audit first to understand the scope of work before committing to a retainer.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
    <h2>Request your audit</h2>

    <p>If your Guildford business is not receiving the search visibility it deserves, an audit is the first step. I identify every problem, rank them by impact, and provide you with a clear path toward improved rankings.</p>

    <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@seo-guildford.uk">hello@seo-guildford.uk</a> with your website URL and I will confirm scope, timeline, and pricing within one working day.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 mt-8 not-prose">
      <a href="/contact/" class="cta-button text-center">Request your audit</a>
      <a href="/free-seo-audit/" class="cta-button-outline text-center">Try the free audit first</a>
    </div>

